Z||000000||fieroshop||04-25-2000||11:14 PM||||It seems that I have about 1000 ft of black walnut veneer and it was going to waste. Since I sold my boat I had no use for or did I. Well I decided to make black walnut panels for my 88 GT. So far I have made about three pieces and have to glue the other pieces to the plastic panels. This veneer is paper thin. So far it looks great. I will post some pictures of my dash when I finish.||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||04-25-2000||11:22 PM||||Well, hell George, I think we can find SOMETHING to do with it. Hmmmm. didja see the post in the OT section about the wooden car for 1/4 million on ebay?  A wood Fiero. Hmmmm. Just thinkin out loud. Don't mind me.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fret Naught||04-27-2000||04:41 PM||||Hey FieroShop,<BR>I build Acoustic Guitars in my spare time, turned out a nice black walnut shift knob and decided to do dash panels. I selected a nice log, sawed it up and now have some 1/8" stock drying. Wish I had some of that Veneer, interested in selling a bit?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||04-27-2000||07:57 PM||||God job George!! I'm still working on 2 sets of carbon fiber dash cover plates, They look good.  <BR>Thanks Gokart for the tips on the clear coat!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> the sample looks better than the ones on the Little Black Toy, but that was my first try, I'm a little better at it now.<P>Still in need of the Aux gauge cover plate (2). And one shifter cover plate.||||reg||1
